-- Source: github.com/reality-farouqk/nigeria-tertiary-institutions-api
-- MIT code, CC0 data (public domain). Snapshot taken 2026-08-30 for this one-time import.
-- No live dependency on the source repo/API is created by this migration.
--
-- Scope: universities only (polytechnics/colleges of education from the same source
-- were NOT imported -- this app models "universities" only; mixing institution types
-- without an institution_type column would misrepresent them).
--
-- Deliberately NOT imported: department-level data. Spot-check found the source-side
-- parser produces wrong output for multi-campus "College X (Location)" entries -- e.g.
-- Osun State University (UNIOSUN) shows 7 "departments" that are actually just campus
-- town names (Osogbo, Ifetedo, Okuku, Ikire, Ipetu-Ijesa, Ejigbo), not real departments.
-- 31 other universities share this naming pattern and were not individually verified.
-- Faculty/college names (one level up) were spot-checked and look reliable -- imported below.
--
-- Known gap: UNIOSUN (pilot university) gets 7 colleges, zero departments. Get the real
-- department list from the SUG and enter it via the admin university management screen
-- (Phase 16) rather than guessing.
--
-- "Courses of study" (source's 4th, explicitly-inferred layer) intentionally skipped entirely.
--
-- Two manual name overrides applied so this doesn't create duplicates of universities
-- already in the table: source's "University of Nigeria" -> kept as "University of Nigeria,
-- Nsukka" (matches existing exact row); source's hyphenated "University of Port-Harcourt"
-- -> normalized to "University of Port Harcourt" (matches existing exact row).

-- 288 universities (28 already existed and are skipped via ON CONFLICT, 260 new), 1340 faculties


